  "id": "COMPOUND:32773 - PROTEIN:6323",
  "verbalization": "Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- is implicated in the target pathway leading to DNA polymerase iota through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for Notoamide B and Plakortide N, both of which are themselves targets of Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-. This implies a hierarchical relationship where the compound influences the activity of these intermediates, which in turn affect DNA polymerase iota. The presence of multiple pathways, each involving different targets, highlights the complexity of the interaction network, but all converge on DNA polymerase iota as the final endpoint. The integration of these pathways underscores the compound's role in modulating the activity of downstream enzymes, potentially through a series of intermediate targets. The mechanism remains somewhat indirect, but the consistent involvement of Notoamide B and Plakortide N as mediators supports a plausible pathway where Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)- exerts its effect via these intermediaries.",
